Law of Large Numbers
\series default
\color inherit
 (
\series bold
\color blue
LLN
\series default
\color inherit
): sample means 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{X}_{n}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}$
\end_inset

 converges to population means 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu=\mathbb{E}_{p}(X)$
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\bar{X}_{n}\overset{p}{\rightarrow}\mathbb{E}_{p}(X)
\]

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $X_{1},\ldots,X_{n}$
\end_inset

 are iid from 
\begin_inset Formula $p(x)$
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset VSpace bigskip
\end_inset


\begin_inset VSpace bigskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\color blue
Central limit theorem
\series default
\color inherit
 (
\series bold
\color blue
CLT
\series default
\color inherit
): informally, for large 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\bar{X}_{n}\overset{\mathrm{approx}}{\sim}N\left(\mu,\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\right),
\]

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma^{2}=\mathbb{V}(X)$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

